#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""macOS-style touchpad gestures for X11.

Reads `libinput debug-events` and provides:

drag   Three-finger drag. A three-finger swipe presses the left button and
       moves the pointer; the button stays held for a short grace period
       after the fingers are lifted so the drag can be resumed. Any one-finger
       motion, click or scroll during the grace period ends the drag.

pinch  Pinch to zoom around the pointer. How each application is driven is
       data, not code: apps.ini maps WM_CLASS names to generic methods, and
       config.ini can override them.
         zoom = touch  Replay the pinch on a virtual uinput touchscreen with
                       one finger on the pointer. Apps that handle
                       touchscreen pinches (Chromium, Electron, some GTK)
                       zoom and pan smoothly around it.
         zoom = wheel  Wheel clicks at the pointer, optionally with a
                       modifier held.
         zoom = keys   Key presses; most apps zoom around their center.
         zoom = none   Leave the pinch alone.
         pan = wheel   Pan with wheel clicks while pinching (wheel/keys).

The daemon must stay resident: libinput does not track touches that were
already on the touchpad when it started.

Runs on Python 3.8 or later with the standard library only.
"""
import sys

